Alana: Heads up — onboarding pain with our Next.js + LangChain starter. Several users hit build/runtime issues: Edge runtime can't use the redis-backed cache we demo, streaming example fails in getServerSideProps, and SDK auth retries behave differently in node vs edge. Any volunteers to make a canonical starter that covers Edge streaming + SSR fallback + LangChain adapter?
Micah: I'm on it. Wasn't parity issue partly from fetch wrapper exposing retry/timeout only in node SDK? We added exponential backoff in v0.8 but Edge bundle strips it.
Sam: I ran into the same when testing on Vercel Edge. Quick workaround: use fetch with manual retry and don't use global AbortController for streaming. Example:

```
async function callRedwood(prompt){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    try{
      const res = await fetch("https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate",{
        method:'POST',
        headers:{'Authorization':`Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}`,'Content-Type':'application/json'},
        body: JSON.stringify({prompt}),
      })
      if(!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status)
      return res
    }catch(e){ if(i===2) throw e }
  }
}
```

Sam: This keeps streaming working on Edge and SSR.
Jordan: For LangChain/LlamaIndex examples we should show both a client-side streaming chat and a server-side reindex flow. I can sketch a small adapter using the new SDK's streaming interface.
Jordan: snippet:

```
import { RedwoodLLM } from 'redwood-sdk'
const llm = new RedwoodLLM({model:'redwood-qa', streaming:true})
await llm.stream((token)=> console.log(token))
```

Alana: Nice. Also need a simple eval harness demo (single-file) that runs locally + in CI and outputs accuracy + rouge.
Maya: I'll own the eval harness. Plan: pytest-like script that runs prompts from /evals and uploads metrics to S3. Want a GH action template that runs on PRs.
Maya: Proposed CI YAML: uses node:18, installs deps, runs `npm run eval -- --ci` and uploads artifact `eval-results.json`.
Micah: Can we add a tiny CLI to scaffold both starters? `npx create-redwood-starter --template nextjs-langchain` — then tests will run in GH action.
Alana: Love it. @dev-bot can you create a repo and PR template? :thumbsup:
